Implement the game of Connect Four, with a graphical interface in pygame. In this game, 2 players take turns dropping discs into a 7 x 6 board until one of them makes 4 in a row horizontally, vertically, or diagonally. The Wikipedia page includes an animation that illustrates how the game works.

To help you get started, I have provided a complete implementation of Tic Tac Toe. You can find a link to it at the end of the last week's lecture notes. Run this program and study it to see how it works. I recommend that you create your Connect Four game by modifying this Tic Tac Toe program.

Your program's graphics should look something like this.

On each player's turn, let them click anywhere in a column to play in the lowest free space in that column. In other words, they should not need to click on the free space itself.

Just like in the Tic Tac Toe program, if a player wins, highlight the winning position like this. On the next click (anywhere), the game should begin again.
